    <statement><p>Consider the three points:</p>
<p><m>A = \left(1,4\right)</m></p>
<p><m>B = \left(5,5\right)</m></p>
<p><m>C = \left(6,7\right)</m>.</p>
<p>Determine the angle between <m>\overline{AB}</m> and <m>\overline{AC}</m>.</p>
<p><m>\theta_a</m>  = <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.295441</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\overrightarrow{AB} = \left\lt 4,1\right&gt;</m> and <m>\overrightarrow{AC} = \left\lt 5,3\right&gt;</m>.



Then, from the identity <m>v \cdotp w = \| v \| \| w \| \cos{\theta}</m> we solve for <m>\theta</m> which yields



<m>\theta = \cos^{-1}{\left( \frac{v \cdotp w}{\| v \| \| w \|} \right)}</m>.



Therefore, <m>\theta_a = \cos^{-1}{\left( \frac{\left\lt 4,1\right&gt; \cdotp \left\lt 5,3\right&gt;}{\| \left\lt 4,1\right&gt; \| \| \left\lt 5,3\right&gt; \|} \right)} = 0.295441</m>.





</solution>
